    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="onb1_title">Every crossing of Lethe costs an obol</string>
    <string name="onb1_text">In the myth, Lethe is the river of forgetting: drink from it and the hours are gone. An endless feed works the same way. Charon will ferry you across, but not for free.</string>
    <string name="onb2_title">Serve the muses, earn obols</string>
    <string name="onb2_text">Calliope pays for reading, Hermes for languages, Athena for learning, Hestia for stillness, Nike for sport. Make your own patrons for anything that matters to you: guitar, code, a side project.</string>
    <string name="onb3_title">Pay Charon for the feed</string>
    <string name="onb3_text">Open Reels or TikTok and Charon waits at the gate. Pay for 5, 15 or 30 minutes, or go by the meter. Night costs more, every crossing after the first costs more, and you can always just turn back.</string>
    <string name="onb4_title">Wake Charon</string>
    <string name="onb4_text">Charon works as an accessibility service: that is how he sees which app and site is open and puts the gate in front of a feed. Find Obol in the list and switch it on.</string>
    <string name="onb4_off">Charon is still asleep</string>
    <string name="onb4_privacy">Everything stays on this phone. Obol has no internet access at all.</string>
    <string name="onb_later">Later</string>
    <string name="onb_begin">Take the first obols</string>

